# Git decides text-vs-binary by sniffing for NUL bytes, and server/scanner.ts
# legitimately contains two: one inside the JUNK_CHARS character class (a
# literal control character, which is why that line carries an eslint
# no-control-regex disable), and one used as a '\0' key separator when keying
# albums by artist+album.
#
# That was enough for git to classify the whole file as binary: `git log -p`
# and GitHub showed "Binary files differ" instead of a diff, grep skipped it
# without saying so, and a merge would have been impossible to resolve except
# by choosing one side wholesale.
#
# Setting `diff` marks these as text even when they contain such bytes;
# `merge` selects the ordinary 3-way text merge. Note this deliberately does
# NOT set the `text` attribute, which would turn on end-of-line normalisation
# and rewrite files on checkout.
*.ts   diff merge
*.tsx  diff merge
